    items: [
      "<strong>v1.20 &mdash; Cross-tenant data-view: admin viewing-as a tenant now sees the tenant&rsquo;s actual data, not their own empty set.</strong> Closes the explicit known limitation v1.19 documented: the admin-bypass shell rendered <code>/app/refill/*</code> chrome for the admin without a real tenant_memberships row, BUT every spa-owner server fn still filtered by <code>verifyAuth(accessToken)</code> userId &mdash; so patient lists, recovery feeds, billing, etc. all came back empty. The admin could walk the chrome but couldn&rsquo;t actually observe the impersonated tenant&rsquo;s work. v1.20 fixes the data layer with an opt-in <code>viewAsUserId</code> parameter on the highest-traffic read fns (Approach C hybrid &mdash; helper + selective opt-in, not a full ~20-fn refactor). <strong>New helper</strong>: <code>resolveEffectiveUserId({ accessToken, viewAsUserId })</code> in <code>src/server/auth-helpers.ts</code>. When viewAsUserId is omitted/null/equal-to-caller, collapses to a plain verifyAuth (zero extra DB hit). When viewAsUserId is provided AND differs from caller, re-verifies admin role server-side against <code>public.user_roles</code> (does NOT trust client-side primaryRole signal) and returns the impersonated user_id as <code>effectiveUserId</code>. Non-admin callers passing viewAsUserId get hard 403 &mdash; the security boundary is the server, not the client. Returns <code>{ effectiveUserId, callerUserId, isViewingAs }</code> so audit logging can use callerUserId while data filters use effectiveUserId. <strong>Server fns opted in</strong> (the page-load fns surfaced on /app/refill/* &mdash; ~8 fns total): <code>listPatients</code>, <code>listOverduePatients</code>, <code>getPatientByKey</code>, <code>getPatientById</code> (patient-ingest.functions.ts) &mdash; the patients-dashboard + detail page surface; <code>listWaitlist</code> (emma-waitlist.functions.ts) &mdash; the /app/refill/rescue waitlist tab; <code>getMyTenantRecoveryFeed</code> (refill-tenants.ts) &mdash; the LiveRecoveryFeed hero widget on RefillHome; <code>getActivePlan</code> + <code>listInvoices</code> (refill-billing.ts) &mdash; the /app/billing read surface. Each schema gets an optional <code>viewAsUserId: z.string().uuid().optional()</code> field; each handler swaps <code>verifyAuth(data.accessToken)</code> for <code>resolveEffectiveUserId({ accessToken: data.accessToken, viewAsUserId: data.viewAsUserId })</code> and uses <code>effectiveUserId</code> for all data filtering. <strong>Intentionally NOT opted in</strong>: write paths (markPatientOptedIn, ingestPatientCsv, applyPricingPlan), Stripe-mutating fns (getPaymentMethodStatus, refill-checkout), summarizeOverdueCohort, listRescueActivity, listPatternAlerts, listRecommendations. Read fns first; admin shouldn&rsquo;t be inadvertently mutating the impersonated tenant&rsquo;s payment method, plan, or patient data. <strong>State shape</strong>: <code>getFirstTenantForAdmin</code> extended to also return <code>ownerUserId</code> &mdash; looks up the tenant_memberships rows for the resolved tenant, prefers the &lsquo;owner&rsquo; role row, falls back to any membership. <code>TenantMembershipState</code>&rsquo;s &lsquo;tenant&rsquo; variant gets an optional <code>viewAsUserId?: string</code> alongside <code>viewAs?: \"admin\"</code> so pages can plumb it without re-querying. <strong>Page-side plumbing</strong>: 5 files updated (<code>app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code>, <code>app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code>, <code>app.refill.rescue.tsx</code>, <code>app.refill.index.tsx</code>, <code>app.billing.tsx</code>) &mdash; each imports useTenantMembership, derives <code>viewAsUserId</code> from the membership state, and passes it as part of every relevant server fn call. Effects re-run when viewAsUserId changes so a mid-session admin walking from one surface to another stays consistent. <code>LiveRecoveryFeed</code> component gets an optional <code>viewAsUserId</code> prop; RefillHome passes <code>membership.viewAsUserId</code> through. Effects re-fire when viewAsUserId changes; realtime channel subscriptions stay scoped to the actual tenantUserIds returned by the server (admin observation does not leak the admin&rsquo;s user_id into the realtime channel filter). <strong>Architectural rationale</strong>: per the v1.19 docblock, the &lsquo;viewAsUserId&rsquo; (tenant-owner&rsquo;s user_id) framing was chosen over &lsquo;viewAsTenantId&rsquo; specifically because spa-owner server fns are historically Emma-era user-scoped (.eq(&lsquo;user_id&rsquo;, userId)). Threading effective user_id preserves that shape verbatim &mdash; no fan-out refactor, no migration. The single tenant-scoped layer (refill-billing.getTenantIdForUser) works identically with the impersonated user_id substituted in. <strong>What&rsquo;s NOT in v1.20 (queued)</strong>: long-tail server fns (~15 more fns under user-id filtering &mdash; listRescueActivity, listPatternAlerts, listRecommendations, summarizeOverdueCohort, etc.) that surface on /app/refill/* but weren&rsquo;t in the top-5 page-load surface; per-fn write-path gating; explicit audit log for admin viewing-as actions. Add the long-tail fns when a specific surface surfaces a regression (admin sees zero rows where there should be data); the helper makes the per-fn addition mechanical (~3 lines per fn). Touched: <code>src/server/auth-helpers.ts</code> (resolveEffectiveUserId + EffectiveUserContext type), <code>src/server/refill-tenants.ts</code> (getFirstTenantForAdmin returns ownerUserId; getMyTenantRecoveryFeed opted in), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (4 fns opted in), <code>src/server/emma-waitlist.functions.ts</code> (listWaitlist opted in), <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> (getActivePlan + listInvoices opted in), <code>src/lib/use-tenant-membership.ts</code> (state shape + admin-fallback wiring), <code>src/components/refill/LiveRecoveryFeed.tsx</code> (prop signature), <code>src/components/refill/RefillHome.tsx</code> (pass through), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code> + <code>$patientId.tsx</code> + <code>app.refill.rescue.tsx</code> + <code>app.refill.index.tsx</code> + <code>app.billing.tsx</code> (page-side plumbing), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
    ],
