      "<strong>v1.17 &mdash; Waitlist toggle off-state actually visible + bigger find: 3 more silently-broken brand tokens.</strong> Grasshopper&rsquo;s screenshot after v1.16 showed the active emerald toggles working but off-state toggles still invisible. Diagnosis was wrong in v1.16: I translated <code>bg-muted</code> &rarr; <code>bg-rule</code> thinking <code>--color-rule</code> existed in <code>@theme</code>. <strong>It didn&rsquo;t.</strong> The only warm-gray token defined in <code>src/styles.css</code> @theme block was <code>--color-border-soft</code>. Every <code>bg-rule</code>, <code>border-rule</code>, <code>bg-rule-soft</code>, <code>hover:bg-rule-soft</code>, <code>divide-rule</code> reference I shipped across v1.10 (Lane 1 polish), v1.14 (/promos port), and v1.16 (patients sweep) has been emitting <strong>zero CSS</strong>. Same class of bug as the original <code>bg-primary</code> find &mdash; just propagated by me, not inherited from openagenticv4. Per <em>feedback-no-blame-no-glide</em>: I confidently translated to brand tokens that didn&rsquo;t exist. <strong>Fix #1 &mdash; define the missing tokens in @theme</strong>: <code>--color-rule: #e6e2d6</code> (matching the existing border-soft for consistency), <code>--color-rule-soft: #f3f0e7</code> (warm off-white for hover/subtle backgrounds), <code>--color-track: #c8c2b3</code> (darker warm-gray with enough contrast against bg-white for switch tracks). Adding these three lines to styles.css <strong>retroactively unblocks every prior polish ship</strong> &mdash; rule-* tokens that were silently broken now render with intent. <strong>Fix #2 &mdash; waitlist toggle off-state</strong>: changed from <code>bg-rule</code> (was broken; would now be subtle <code>#e6e2d6</code> which is too low-contrast against bg-white card) to <code>bg-track</code> (the new darker <code>#c8c2b3</code>) for an iOS-style switch with visible track contrast matching the agentiport reference Grasshopper screenshot-pinned. <strong>Fix #3 &mdash; A-list star fill</strong>: another silently-broken token found mid-walk &mdash; <code>fill-primary</code> on active VIP stars never rendered (primary undefined per v1.10-v1.11 finding). Translated to <code>fill-emerald</code> so VIP-flagged patients now show a filled emerald star. <strong>Strategic note</strong>: this is the third class of silently-broken tokens (after <code>primary</code> in v1.10 and <code>card</code>/<code>border</code>/<code>muted</code>/<code>foreground</code> in v1.14/v1.16). A wider audit of refill-app&rsquo;s actual <code>@theme</code> contents vs all token references in code is now warranted &mdash; would surface every additional silently-emitted-zero-CSS class name in one pass. Queued as a Lane 2 backlog item. Touched: <code>src/styles.css</code> (3 new @theme lines), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code> (toggle off-state token + star fill token), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
