      "<strong>v1.10 &mdash; Lane 1 polish sweep on /app/billing (brand-coherent + softer rhythm + a silently-broken-token find).</strong> Five Lane 1 backlog items in one ship, all on <code>app.billing.tsx</code>. <strong>(1) Card corner radius</strong>: every <code>rounded-2xl</code> on the page &rarr; <code>rounded-xl</code>. Softer rhythm that matches the RefillHome quick-action cards (the canonical Refill house style) instead of the sharper platform-y radius the page inherited from the emma-era surface. Eight sites touched (active-plan banner, no-active amber banner, plan cards, empty invoice state, invoice table container, card-on-file states 1+2+3). <strong>(2) Brand amber tokens replace Tailwind generic</strong>: the &lsquo;No active plan yet&rsquo; banner + the Hybrid plan-card icon accent + the &lsquo;Sent&rsquo; invoice-status pill + the test-mode footnote on Card-on-file used Tailwind&rsquo;s generic <code>amber-500</code>/<code>amber-700</code> (orange-leaning, doesn&rsquo;t match the muted goldenrod established by Refill brand). Swapped for the brand tokens <code>bg-amber-soft</code> (<code>#fdf6dc</code>) and <code>text-amber</code> (<code>#8a6d0c</code>) defined in <code>@theme</code>. <strong>(3) Refresh button chip-style</strong>: the PageHeader actions-slot refresh button used shadcn <code>border-border</code> + <code>text-ink-soft</code> tokens (generic). Now uses the inactive RefillNav chip pattern (transparent bg, <code>#5a6068</code> ink, <code>#e6e2d6</code> border, 12px semibold) via inline style &mdash; matches the chip row Karen sees up top, reads as &lsquo;sibling not stranger.&rsquo; <strong>(4) Section labels sentence-cased</strong>: &ldquo;PICK YOUR PLAN&rdquo; and &ldquo;INVOICE HISTORY&rdquo; both shed <code>uppercase tracking-wider</code> and the <code>text-sm</code> bump to a softer <code>text-[15px] font-semibold</code>. Refill voice is warmer than enterprise-form-label all-caps; this is the consumer-feel sweep. Table column headers KEEP their all-caps (compact scan-friendly is the right call for dense table heads). The &lsquo;Active&rsquo; chip on plan cards also keeps uppercase &mdash; chip indicators reading uppercase is genre-correct, not the same complaint as section labels. <strong>(5) BIG FIND &mdash; bg-primary is a silently-broken token in this theme</strong>: <code>styles.css</code>&rsquo;s <code>@theme</code> block defines emerald, ink, amber, paper, rose &mdash; but NOT primary. Every <code>bg-primary</code> / <code>text-primary</code> / <code>border-primary</code> / <code>bg-primary/5</code> / <code>bg-primary/15</code> reference in the codebase is a no-op generating no CSS at all (Tailwind v4 only emits utilities for colors in the active theme). On <code>app.billing.tsx</code> alone there were 6 such broken references (active-plan banner border + bg, plan-card active state, primary-tone icon, Active-pill, Pick-Performance button bg, Add-payment-method button bg). All swapped to the brand emerald equivalents: <code>border-emerald</code> + <code>bg-emerald-soft</code>, <code>bg-emerald</code> + <code>text-paper</code>. The visible difference is significant &mdash; what was rendering as default-text-color or transparent now reads as the sage emerald that&rsquo;s supposed to anchor the page. <strong>Repo-wide cleanup of remaining</strong> <code>bg-primary</code> <strong>references is a queued follow-on ship</strong> (many other pages affected; out of v1.10 scope). Also nudged: <code>text-emerald-700</code>/<code>emerald-500/15</code> on card-on-file flipped to brand <code>text-emerald</code>/<code>bg-emerald</code>. Touched: <code>src/routes/app.billing.tsx</code> (~18 surgical edits), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
