      "<strong>v1.7 &mdash; Stripe invoice push + auto-charge (Phase B-lite of the $$ loop).</strong> v1.6 captured the card; v1.7 actually uses it. <code>generateMonthlyInvoiceForTenant</code> in <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> now extends past the DB-draft write: when the upserted row has <code>total_due_usd &gt; 0</code> AND the tenant has a <code>stripe_customer_id_{mode}</code> AND a card on file AND no existing <code>stripe_invoice_id</code> on the row, it (1) creates a Stripe <code>InvoiceItem</code> for the total amount, (2) creates a Stripe <code>Invoice</code> with <code>collection_method:&quot;charge_automatically&quot;</code> + <code>default_payment_method</code> set to the saved card + <code>auto_advance:true</code>, (3) calls <code>finalizeInvoice</code> &mdash; which synchronously triggers the charge attempt against the saved card. On success the DB row stamps <code>stripe_invoice_id</code> and flips <code>status</code> to <code>&quot;sent&quot;</code> (or <code>&quot;paid&quot;</code> if Stripe cleared the charge in the same call), plus <code>sent_at</code> / <code>paid_at</code>. Idempotency keys (<code>refill_inv_&lt;tenant&gt;_&lt;period&gt;_item</code> / <code>_invoice</code>) prevent duplicate Stripe Invoices on cron retry within Stripe&rsquo;s 24h window; DB idempotency on <code>(tenant_id, period_start)</code> + the <code>stripe_invoice_id IS NULL</code> guard prevent re-push on long-lag retries. Push failures are caught and logged but non-fatal &mdash; the DB row stays at <code>draft</code> so the next cron run retries; the spa-side state stays correct (Karen sees the draft, knows it didn&rsquo;t charge yet). Webhook-driven sent&rarr;paid flips on <code>invoice.paid</code> / <code>invoice.payment_failed</code> are Phase B-full&rsquo;s job; for now the truthful state lives in Stripe and Karen can verify via the Manage button (Stripe Customer Portal) which always shows the real status. <strong>Manual-trigger / testing</strong>: <code>/api/cron/refill-invoice</code> now accepts <code>?period=YYYY-MM</code> as a query-param override for the prior-month default &mdash; useful for firing against the current month&rsquo;s verified events without waiting for the 1st-of-next-month natural cron. Production cron leaves the param off and gets the prior-month behavior unchanged. Comment block on the route + the doc-block on <code>generateMonthlyInvoicesForAll</code> updated to reflect the new behavior. Touched: <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> (Stripe push branch + periodMonth optional arg + Stripe import already present from v1.6), <code>src/routes/api.cron.refill-invoice.ts</code> (period query param + doc-block).",
