      "<strong>v1.6 &mdash; Stripe payment-method capture wired end-to-end (Phase A of the $$ loop).</strong> The Refill Stripe surface had been built but never connected: <code>/api/refill-checkout</code> (264 lines, setup-mode + subscription-mode), <code>/api/refill-portal</code> (127 lines, Customer Portal session), mode-aware <code>stripe_customer_id_{test,live}</code> columns on tenants, monthly invoice cron, Stripe webhook handler &mdash; all sitting there, all unreachable from the UI. The Billing page&rsquo;s &lsquo;Pick a plan&rsquo; button called <code>applyPricingPlan</code> (DB-only) and stopped there, so no Stripe Customer was ever created, no card was ever captured, and the footer disclaimer literally read &lsquo;v366.x adds the Stripe customer + auto-pay flow when you&rsquo;re ready.&rsquo; This ship is that v366.x. <strong>Three additions:</strong> <strong>(1)</strong> New <code>getPaymentMethodStatus</code> server fn in <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> &mdash; reads the mode-aware customer id from tenants, calls <code>stripe.customers.listPaymentMethods</code>, returns <code>{ hasCardOnFile, brand, last4, expMonth, expYear, stripeMode }</code>. Best-effort: failures don&rsquo;t take down the rest of the billing page. <strong>(2)</strong> New <code>CardOnFileSection</code> component rendered on <code>/app/billing</code> between the active-plan banner and the plan selector. Three states: loading spinner, emerald-tinted &lsquo;Card on file &middot; Visa &middot;&middot; 4242 &middot; expires MM/YY&rsquo; with a Manage CTA (opens Stripe Customer Portal), or the neutral &lsquo;No card on file yet&rsquo; row with a sage primary &lsquo;Add payment method&rsquo; CTA. <strong>(3)</strong> Wired the CTAs: Add-card POSTs to <code>/api/refill-checkout</code> with <code>plan: &quot;starter&quot;</code> always (setup mode, no charge regardless of which plan the spa is on &mdash; per [[project-trial-first-no-money-asks]], the card just sits on file until the first verified-recovery invoice runs); Manage POSTs to <code>/api/refill-portal</code>. Both redirect via <code>window.location.href = body.url</code>. Return URL handler: <code>?upgrade=success</code> toasts &lsquo;Card on file. You&rsquo;re all set.&rsquo; and refreshes; <code>?upgrade=cancelled</code> toasts the no-pressure message; both strip the search params via <code>replaceState</code> so a refresh doesn&rsquo;t re-trigger the toast. Footer disclaimer rewritten from &lsquo;coming soon&rsquo; to the live-now Stripe-hosted-checkout reassurance. Test-mode badge surfaces under the card row when <code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code> starts with <code>sk_test_</code>. <strong>What this Phase A does NOT do</strong> (queued for next ships): Phase B &mdash; the monthly invoice cron still ships <code>refill_invoices</code> rows as DB drafts; pushing them to Stripe + finalize + auto-charge against the saved card is the next milestone. Phase C &mdash; trial-end + post-recovery drip CTAs that nudge card capture without disrupting onboarding. Touched: <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> (new fn + Stripe import), <code>src/routes/app.billing.tsx</code> (imports, state, two handlers, return-URL effect, section render, component definition).",
